  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Circle $x^2+y^2-4 x-8 y-5=0$\nCentre $=(2,4)$, Radius $=\\sqrt{4+16+5}=5$\nIf circle is intersecting line $3 x-4 y=m$\nat two distinct points.\n$\\Rightarrow$ length of perpendicular from centre $ < $ radius\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{|6-16-\\mathrm{m}|}{5} < 5$\n$\\Rightarrow|10+\\mathrm{m}| < 25$\n$\\Rightarrow-25 < m+10 < 25$\n$\\Rightarrow-35 < \\mathrm{m} < 15$.",
    "image": null
  },
